  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[WARNING! SPIDERS IN THE VIDEO ]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2000,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why are the most venomous species found in the warmest places on Earth? I mean, take Australia for example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8280,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Depending on who you ask, it has all or nearly all of the ten most venomous snakes in the world,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14259,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus the funnel-Web spider, the blue ringed octopus, box jellyfish,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18580,
    "dDurationMs": 6529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paralysis tick and stonefish, all found in Australia, are the most lethal of their kind and even this cute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25210,
    "dDurationMs": 1819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "platypus has an ankle spur,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27029,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which in the male, secretes a venom that can kill a dog. In humans it would merely cause excruciating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33370,
    "dDurationMs": 7639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pain. This question, why do the most venomous species live in the warmest places, is one that I've wondered about for most of my life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41379,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps it's because I was born here in the small town of Traralgon, Australia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45989,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the first house where I ever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48820,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lived. As my mum recalls {Derek's Mum}\"in the backyard there was a shade where we found red backs,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54399,
    "dDurationMs": 5930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I used to play in the shed? {Derek's Mum}\"I don't think once we found the red backs that we let you in there.\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60329,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, that's very comforting. Thanks mum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62649,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you don't know what a red back is, it's a very poisonous spider. Hold up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66330,
    "dDurationMs": 6629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I gotta tell past Derek something. You see it's important that we say venomous and not poisonous because poisonous means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72960,
    "dDurationMs": 5069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it'll be harmful if you eat it, whereas venomous means it'll try to eat you and that will be harmful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78759,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Continue. So thankfully they never bit me, otherwise, I wouldn't be standing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82860,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83360,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here today. Now before we go any further,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85020,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's probably worth asking, is it true, do more venomous species really live in hot places?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90970,
    "dDurationMs": 3222,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well apparently I'm not the only one who thinks so because I found this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94192,
    "dDurationMs": 2677,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reddit thread on the topic. Though, it really didn't explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96869,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why that was the case. But what about the data? Well, here is a map of the global average temperatures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103420,
    "dDurationMs": 5870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Compare that with this map that I've colored in according to the number of venomous species in each country."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109659,
    "dDurationMs": 6559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The country with the most venomous species is Mexico with eighty different organisms with the power to kill you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116469,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's followed closely by Brazil and then Australia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120250,
    "dDurationMs": 3769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well this seems to all match up very well with the global average temperatures."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124180,
    "dDurationMs": 7790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why is it so? My first hypothesis was that there's something about the heat which enables the formation of these venom molecules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132190,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I ran that idea past Professor Polyakov of Periodic Videos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136240,
    "dDurationMs": 5809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "{Professor Polyakov}\"no intent filter\" [alright] \"because the reason is that if you go up a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142780,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ten degrees centigrade change in temperature round about room temperature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147940,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[okay], will only double the rate of most chemical reactions and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152800,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't think anything evolutionary is likely to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159490,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolve to such a big difference based on just a factor of two in the rates.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163780,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So maybe it's worth asking what are these venom molecules exactly?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167770,
    "dDurationMs": 3679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in most species where the venom is delivered by fangs it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171449,
    "dDurationMs": 1471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolved from saliva. In the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173290,
    "dDurationMs": 4046,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funnel-web spider for example, the lethal effect seems quite accidental."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177336,
    "dDurationMs": 2304,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you've got to understand about venom,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179830,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's there, it's a secondary thing that it actually kills. The actual reason that spiders have got venom is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187090,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to digest their prey. That they happen to do most of it before they actually eat it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193210,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Injecting the venom and the venom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195550,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will start to liquefy whatever they've caught and,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199990,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once it's turned to liquid,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202660,
    "dDurationMs": 6619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all spiders live on soup. The funnel-web evolved without any humans or other primates around and yet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ironically, its venom is most potent for exactly this group. Biggest  evolutionary joke ever,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215710,
    "dDurationMs": 3889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only group of animals with backbones"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220390,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's actually allergic to their venom are the primates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224590,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't have primates in Australia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227350,
    "dDurationMs": 2929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right, so it's lemurs, monkeys, apes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231310,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232250,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thus most species deliver, not just one type of venom molecule"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236380,
    "dDurationMs": 6119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a whole cocktail of different proteins that range in length from short chain to very long chain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242660,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243160,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and these molecules can serve a range of functions. Some are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246726,
    "dDurationMs": 2913,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "neurotoxins which can disable your nervous system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250040,
    "dDurationMs": 3718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Others are hemotoxins which actually attack your blood cells and can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253758,
    "dDurationMs": 3171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dissolve tissues, but since we're talking about cocktails,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257000,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what would happen if you drank some venom? You could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260750,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take a vial of taipan venom and happily have it with your scotch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264070,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it wouldn't be a problem as long as you didn't have any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267620,
    "dDurationMs": 3417,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "irritation on the mucosal lining or any stomach ulcer or things like this. It's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271037,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got to get into the bloodstream to be a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273070,
    "dDurationMs": 2849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so since drinking the venom is not gonna kill you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276070,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what should you do if you get bitten by say an inland taipan?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280310,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the world's most venomous land snake. What you do? Don't panic. Stay calm."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285010,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that would be easier said than done. The venom travels through the lymphatic system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289310,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it doesn't usually travel through the veins or the blood vessels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292630,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that's just quite close on under the skin, and if it reaches your nervous system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297020,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it'll shut down the signaling pathways that keep your heart beating and your lungs breathing, and so what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303560,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually kills you is suffocation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305720,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what you need to do is stay very still and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308450,
    "dDurationMs": 4219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bandage up the limb that's been bitten from the tip all the way back to your torso."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312890,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the bandage needs to be really tight to trap the venom within the lymphatic system,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317419,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not so tight as to cut off the blood flow to the limb."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321979,
    "dDurationMs": 5570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now once you've got it bandaged up, you need to find some anti-venom. What is anti-venom?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327830,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328330,
    "dDurationMs": 4702,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's made by injecting a large organism like a horse with a dilute solution of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333032,
    "dDurationMs": 2678,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the venom. The horse then produces antibodies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335930,
    "dDurationMs": 4525,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for that venom which you can harvest and inject into yourself in case you get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340455,
    "dDurationMs": 3115,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bitten. Making anti-venom is tough work. It would take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343760,
    "dDurationMs": 7039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seventy milkings of a funnel-web spider to get enough venom to make a single dose of anti-venom and what's worse"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351260,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anti-venom can only be used on an individual a limited number of times because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356060,
    "dDurationMs": 6559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over those uses your body will build up antibodies to the anti-venom making the anti-venom ineffective."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362870,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might wonder well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364240,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why can't you just inject yourself with dilute amounts of venom and build up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368590,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your own antibodies to the venom? That would work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371900,
    "dDurationMs": 5119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except for the fact that when you get bitten you need to have a lot of antibodies in your system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377020,
    "dDurationMs": 6660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to keep your antibodies at that high level you would need to keep injecting yourself with the venom, say every month"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383680,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's probably not the best thing for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386870,
    "dDurationMs": 5269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why is it that people in warm climates need to worry about this and not people in cold climates?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392360,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I went to the experts to find out about this trend. You know broadly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397040,
    "dDurationMs": 6169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yeah, there's really not much of a pattern happening. Really? What about that reddit thread and the map"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403210,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I made? If you're saying, is there a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405200,
    "dDurationMs": 3379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "global pattern showing that you get more venomous animals in hot places,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408580,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't know if there is. In snakes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410680,
    "dDurationMs": 3179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the group that I'm most familiar with, in Australia the pattern is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414200,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diametric reverse of that one. If you wander around Southern Australia,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418431,
    "dDurationMs": 1668,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every snake you find on that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420110,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kosciusko is venomous. If you wander around the tropics of Darwin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423440,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're very unlikely to see a venomous snake. They're all pythons and harmless colubrid snakes. Now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428380,
    "dDurationMs": 3149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is unexpected. The most venomous snakes in Australia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431810,
    "dDurationMs": 5089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live in the coldest places and the reason for that is? 20 million years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437360,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an itinerant sea snake coming down from Asia as Australia drifted up to Asia, got to Australia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443180,
    "dDurationMs": 4122,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was venomous to start with. There were no snakes in Australia at the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447302,
    "dDurationMs": 1568,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time and so venomous snakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449090,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "radiated through Australia. This big family called the elapid II the Cobra family. Okay,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453220,
    "dDurationMs": 3217,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but on a global scale, my point remains. There are more venomous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456437,
    "dDurationMs": 2212,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "species in hot countries. There's gonna be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458810,
    "dDurationMs": 5299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vastly more venomous snakes in a warm climate area than in a cold climate area. The problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464110,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that there's vastly more snakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465950,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as a proportion of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467930,
    "dDurationMs": 4309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "snakes that are there, the venomous guys are probably going to be about the same and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472310,
    "dDurationMs": 4279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe even less in the case of a place like Australia than they would be in a cold area."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476690,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why are there more venomous species in warm places?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479720,
    "dDurationMs": 4651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the truth is there aren't, at least not as a proportion of species. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484371,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "majority of venomous species on Earth are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487220,
    "dDurationMs": 4759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ectotherms. Those are organisms whose body temperatures are regulated by their surroundings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492680,
    "dDurationMs": 3974,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that means that they can only really have short bursts of energy, so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496654,
    "dDurationMs": 3036,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of chasing down prey and running away from predators,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500000,
    "dDurationMs": 5869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they needed a different strategy to allow them to survive and so many of them evolved venom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506210,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is a greater diversity of ectotherms in warm climates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509620,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it only stands to reason that there will be a greater number of venomous species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513710,
    "dDurationMs": 3319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's not to say that there aren't venomous species in cold places."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517339,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only snakes that get into the arctic circle are European vipers, a venomous species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522050,
    "dDurationMs": 5059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But biodiversity alone isn't the complete answer to this question. It also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527480,
    "dDurationMs": 750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "depends on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528230,
    "dDurationMs": 3945,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolutionary history. If you had come to Australia 20 million years ago, there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532175,
    "dDurationMs": 3035,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would have been no snakes at all. The venomous ones got here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535210,
    "dDurationMs": 3416,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first and the non-venomous came after. I think it's a really lousy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538626,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explanation, but it's the best one that we've got."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542300,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is that a lousy explanation? Well it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545839,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547339,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "invite any lovely complicated piece of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550490,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ecological theory or anything else."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551830,
    "dDurationMs": 1509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just relying on history."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553339,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is a pattern that's very strong and doesn't seem to be explicable any other way and nowadays in Hawaii"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559180,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are no venomous snakes and the same goes for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561680,
    "dDurationMs": 4275,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jamaica. These are warm places that just haven't evolved or have lost any"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565955,
    "dDurationMs": 2225,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "venomous snakes that they may have had."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568430,
    "dDurationMs": 1813,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it might just be a lucky accident"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570243,
    "dDurationMs": 3726,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we've been fortunate enough to be blessed with a few venomous spiders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574250,
    "dDurationMs": 2179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am also reminded that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576430,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're living in a particular point in time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578839,
    "dDurationMs": 5210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly 15,000 years after the last ice age. Now that would have wiped a lot of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 584209,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ectotherms from the Northern Latitudes of the Northern Hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587510,
    "dDurationMs": 5209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, in Ireland there are no snakes because the place was wiped clean by an ice sheet and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593240,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "snakes haven't managed to get back to the island yet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595720,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My point is the distribution of species depends on what happened. It may be an unsatisfying explanation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602140,
    "dDurationMs": 4709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I'd rather know the truth than just believe in a trend that's not actually there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607370,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Really?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608450,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[you're] a decimal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609550,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What do you think is gonna happen to the spot on the screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611800,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as I narrow...  The color of the blue morpho is created by the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614990,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "structure of its scales"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616910,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is what you do - butterflies?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618940,
    "dDurationMs": 6570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But see all your organs [are] where the signs are getting lost - wings makes mathletes [a] trap the light and if you should not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625510,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flare out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626540,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would never realize with the size learns and certainty [prints] directed alert so..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630265,
    "dDurationMs": 3475,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As I started to go through this big investigation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634009,
    "dDurationMs": 6231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I realize just how complicated this is and how many mysteries are still out there. For example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 640250,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why are some species deadly venomous and in others the venom is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644199,
    "dDurationMs": 3071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is pretty weak, and I didn't end up with anything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648450,
    "dDurationMs": 5539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The deadly guys turned out to have ecologies that are very similar to the guys with very weak venom and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654300,
    "dDurationMs": 3619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it may be a historical accident. Another strange observation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657920,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that a lot of snakes that have evolved more recently have actually lost the ability to produce venom. The big success story in snakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665360,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worldwide are the harmless ones. They've actually evolved from venomous snakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669960,
    "dDurationMs": 3769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Venom is an ancestral characteristic in modern snakes. The"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674400,
    "dDurationMs": 2869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "successful snakes are the ones that left it behind and they gave it up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677270,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they're proliferated despite not having venom,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680130,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Apparently the cost of making venom isn't much more than the cost of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682130,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making saliva."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684890,
    "dDurationMs": 5849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it seems curious that they would lose what seems to be a killer advantage over other species."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691110,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have thoughts about this or any other mysteries regarding the global"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695050,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "distribution of venomous species put them in the comments below."
    } ]
  } ]
}
